{"scenario":"sis-flow-off-reset-by-unbind","rows":["S-0019","S-0027","S-0163","A-0037","A-0260","C-1050"],"source":"Ed4 S.4.1, p.S-5","description":"Flow control goes with the binding: a client held off by S_DATA_FLOW_OFF that unbinds and binds again has flow on with no S_DATA_FLOW_ON, and the U_PDUs it sent before do not count against it.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":256,"block_ms":4800}]}},"note":"Channel held busy from 0 (P5-4), so nothing goes on air (K-0066). Conn 1 binds SAP 5 for non-ARQ and its eight 2048-byte U_PDUs to 0.0.1.3 at 0 (TTL 30, so TTD 60000) bring it to eight MTUs and S_DATA_FLOW_OFF, as in sis/flow-off-discard-rejected (interp S-0163). At 1000 it unbinds (A-0037, no answer) and binds SAP 5 again: S_BIND_ACCEPTED and no S_DATA_FLOW_ON, since flow is on for a new binding (interp S-0027), and the U_PDUs of the old binding, still queued in the DTS (A-0260), no longer count against it (interp S-0163). So \u0027again\u0027, TTL 10 (TTD 21000), is accepted, not discarded, and restarts dts.ttd for the new earliest TTD (C-1050). At 21000 the DTS rejects it for TTL and re-arms dts.ttd for 60000; at 60000 it rejects the eight old C_PDUs. Neither expiry sends S_DATA_FLOW_ON: flow is already on and the old U_PDUs count against nobody."}
